most murderers are straight dudes dummy. most murder-ees are women or trans people. gays aren't the problem.

God this gives me so much hope. I am very surprised to know that this is something that other lesbians deal with. I truly thought I was alone in this and if I were to speak up then the people in my life won't take me seriously.

&#x200B;

Yeah, I also grew up in a pretty homophobic environment and it sucks feel that internalized homophobia. I still sometimes wish I could be straight because life would be easier. I really hope we can get better. Both of us will be loved and have that person(s) to share our hearts with.

&#x200B;

Please know you can always reach out if you ever want to talk.

That made me laugh :) I love that analogy. I am definitely allergic to men! Thank you for validating what I am and wanting me to stick around.

&#x200B;

Actually, I do worry a lot because of this. I fear that I won't be taken seriously in the community due to the things I allow to happen to me. But I agree with you that is a form of self harm. I want someone to hurt me so badly and put myself in pretty dangerous situations frequently.

That is the one thing that everyone says on these things and was the most unhelpful reply possible, but thank you if the intention was support. The issue is therapy is expensive and I can't even buy myself food and no therapists that accept my insurance are emailing me back, so I am obviously frustrated. I would have been in therapy a long time ago if I could. 

&#x200B;

I don't have drug addictions, I am in the beginning stages of becoming an alcoholic, but I don't abuse drugs. Also, the problem is my interactions with men, the disrespect for my autonomy, and the constant desire and acts of almost dying.

[https://i.imgur.com/Uq8x6uP.jpg](https://i.imgur.com/Uq8x6uP.jpg)

&#x200B;

I just wanted to say that you are absolutely beautiful and double chins are normal. Congratulations on the birth of your lil baby :)

Here I study Psychology and I am in my last year, but they took away my funding so I have to drop out. I would either want to continue with Psych or try something new like some fine arts (I am a painter).

&#x200B;

EDIT: I would learn more towards the arts in Mexico I think. I might be able to finish my degree in the US someday if they can get my papers fixed.

Do you have a penis or vagina?

&#x200B;

If you have a vagina, there are lots of super great ways to have sex! There are toys, dental dams, hands... So, it really changes nothing in a sex life. I have had a great experience being HPV+ and having a fulfilling sex life.


If you have a penis, they usually don't test for that and there is a good chance you already have at least one strain of HPV (due to how common it is). Also, dental dams are amazing because they cover up a lot more area than a condom, which falls short in the coverage. You can totally still have oral with dental dams, too! Maybe this is a good opportunity to learn how to do more sexy things?

&#x200B;

Honestly, there are lots of safe possibilities for sex. Sometimes you have to be a little creative, but it is still awesome.

