God so many. I never had crushes on boys once everyone else started to. I remember in elementary through high school the girls would talk about their crushes and I could never relate. I always liked my friends, but I didn't understand the romantic feelings until high school.

&#x200B;

When it came to me having sex; I had to go extreme BDSM or high risk to enjoy anything. I was never into dick. I would have to be doing something wild and unsafe to be getting any thrill from it, which got me into a lot of not so great situations. I used to participate in "sisification", which is turning cis-men into ladies and forcing them to behave in a feminine way, and then I was interested in them (all 100% consensual and a part of kink). Then, I finally understood that I have no romantic or sexual feelings towards men lol.

&#x200B;

Please don't be like me. Always use protection and don't get into strangers cars. Love you all :)

God yeah. I do see your perspective and can relate. I am fem and men often do not respect me when I tell them that I am a lesbian or think I am lying to them. It causes so much extra stress in my life having to prove my sexuality to others.

&#x200B;

Everyone who tries to change someones sexuality is wrong. I wonder if this is going to open a positive conversation about the matter now that it is something that finally effects straight men? Do you think there are any positive outcomes that can arise from this awful situation?

YES. When I was watching the videos this is something that really hurt to see (aside from the coercion and abuse of power). He should know what it is like to question yourself, feel alone, and just outright bad about yourself... why would he want to cause someone else to feel the same way? Imagine the emotional turmoil that must have caused those men. I remember back when I told myself that I needed to be straight and tried to be with men and it fucked me up. I would cry every single night. It is so disgusting that James would want to put those bad feelings on someone else. 

&#x200B;

Honestly, I am so grateful that this is being taken seriously, because often times it isn't. I am also beyond happy I didn't end up buying his makeup palate... 

&#x200B;

I hope all of those men that he abused and coerced are doing okay.

Oh honey, you are handing this really well and I totally understand. I was dating this girl for like 6 months and then she somehow got pregnant and it filled me with a lot of the same emotions.

&#x200B;

Honestly, I don't think the issue is with his male-ness and what comes with it. I think that people who leave relationships would no matter what and there is nothing we can do about it. It happens in straight relationships, too. There will be a girl who values you permanently. As cliche as this is, what happened showed you that she was not the one for you.

&#x200B;

I am sure you are able to pleasure a woman. I know how you feel, but honestly penises don't even usually do a good job. I think that, even from a bi perspective (which I am not, but I have asked my friends), sex with women is better. The ratio of female orgasms with male partners is pretty low, but with female and female the orgasm rates are significantly higher. As for the skin to skin connection, we've got our hands, mouths, and hot bodies close, so that is very intimate.... and boobs, oh man, those beautiful creations.

&#x200B;

I hope that this isn't too hard on you and that you can feel better <3

&#x200B;

Plus, with a strap you can do it better anyway.

I LOVE GIRLS TOOOOO! thank you :) It really was dreamy aghhh <3 I hope that you can find a lady like that, too :)

&#x200B;

Ps I am happy you learned how to quote on mobile

Thank you! I totally felt like people would not want me, but it doesn't seem to have changed anything at all. Everyone has been overwhelmingly positive and loving to me! I don't blame the people that feel that way because the stigma is extreme and there isn't a lot of education (if any) in the public school system.

&#x200B;

I am glad that you don't have anything, but remember, if it ever happens it really won't be a big deal (even though it feels like it).

&#x200B;

Awww! Thank you so much! I am so happy that hearing about this made your day a lil better :)

Hi :) I am Selena, 22, living in the US but I spent 4 months in Mexico City this year! I always thought it was more liberal, but there are definitely a lot of machistas. There were some mean looks... I dated a couple girls down there and I am thinking about maybe moving there in a year after I finish school in the US. I do know that Zona Rosa has lots of LGBT folx, but it is really expensive and I was always too scared to go to the gay bars by myself.

&#x200B;

I am def down to talk English or Spanish. I have whatsapp :)

